# Card catalog merges

When copying or updating animal entries between `data/card_catalog.json` and `data/card_catalog (2) copy.json` (or other catalog JSON files):

- **Match on `name`**, not `id`.
- After merging into the full copy catalog, renumber `id` sequentially (0..n-1) if the user asks to adjust ids.
- Do not assume `card_catalog.json` slot ids (e.g. 1, 10, 20) match positions in the full catalog after renumbering.

Example (Node):

```javascript
const byName = Object.fromEntries(source.animals.map((a) => [a.name, a]));
data.animals = data.animals.map((animal) =>
  byName[animal.name] ? { ...byName[animal.name], id: animal.id } : animal
);
```

When pulling from the small catalog into the full catalog, preserve the full catalog entry’s `id` unless renumbering is requested.
